n and if we act i think  we will be as confident as we can be and  i think that's the responsibility on the  government today it will be a  cross-party uh responsibility as well um  and i can i can commit to those  recommendations those must do's uh as  i'm sure sajid javid the health  secretary will will be holding into  account as the opposition but we'll also  be taking it on board in terms of our  own plans uh you know for the next  general election where we hope labour  will be in government will you from  friday will you be testing if you've got  um covert symptoms yeah i think people  should and to be honest so they can't  afford to well that's the that's the big  question isn't it kay i think what's  what's effectively happening now is is a  stealth tax it's a covered tax on people  doing the right things i'm glad that  finally the government's seen sense and  said that nhs staff will get access to  free testing  but but but what about what about  families that will struggle to pay for  the test what about those people that  are going regularly into care homes to  see their parents or grandparents and  will want to do the right thing before  going in you know we've got rising bills  we know the cost of living is a big  issue and we've got big tax rise coming  in april 2 which will hit families so on  top of this to add an additional cost  whilst lecturing the public on personal  responsibility when it comes to covert  which is in itself is laughable given  the actions of the prime minister we've  got to make sure that people can afford  to do the right thing and that's why i  think it's the wrong decision at the  wrong time to take away access to free  testing now i've been reading my notes  have you because i was going to go on to  ask you about what happened uh with as  far as partier is concerned we've had  the first tranche of fines 20 separate  fines don't know how many people but 20  separate fines have been issued people  were breaking the law at the 